        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ದಿನಚರಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದಿನಚರಿ — dinacari — \"a diary\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಜ್ಜಿ ಪ್ರತಿದಿನ ರಾತ್ರಿ ದಿನಚರಿ ಬರೆಯುತ್ತಿದ್ದರು. ajji pratidina rātri dinacari bareyuttiddaru. Grandmother used to write her diary every night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ದಿನಚರಿಗಳು, dinacarigaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also means a daily routine: ನನ್ನ ದಿನಚರಿ (dinacari) ಬೆಳಗ್ಗೆ ಆರು ಗಂಟೆಗೆ ಶುರು."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ದಿನಚರಿ (dinacari) is borrowed from Sanskrit dinacaryā, \"daily work\" (Monier-Williams), from dina \"a day\" and caryā \"conduct\" (CDIAL 4710)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
